  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7222_008",
    "query": "Can a business provide statistical comparison data (such as output percentiles) when responding to a consumer's ADMT access request?",
    "target_section": "7222",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "HYBRID_BOTH",
    "route_correct": false,
    "route_reasoning": "Query contains ambiguous update keyword 'comparison'. Routing to hybrid policy + diff lookup.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.5,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Yes. Under \u00a7 7222(l), nothing prohibits a business from providing voluntary additional explanatory information, such as the range of possible outputs or aggregate output statistics (e.g., the top five most common outputs and the percentage of consumers receiving each in the past calendar year) to help consumers compare their outcome.",
    "generated_answer": "Yes, a business is permitted to provide statistical comparison data to a consumer when responding to a request to access Automated Decisionmaking Technology (ADMT).\n\n### Current Compliance Requirements\nAccording to **\u00a7 7222(l)**, nothing in the regulations prohibits a business from providing additional information to help a consumer understand how ADMT was used to make a significant decision regarding them. \n\nSpecifically, the business may provide:\n*   The range of possible outputs.\n*   Aggregate output statistics to help the consumer understand how they compare to other consumers (e.g., the five most common outputs and the percentage of consumers who received each of those outputs during the preceding calendar year).\n\n### Amendment Context\nThese provisions were introduced as part of the 2026 regulatory updates regarding ADMT. Prior to these updates, the regulations did not contain specific requirements or permissions regarding \"Requests to Access ADMT\" or the definition of \"Automated Decisionmaking Technology\" (\u00a7 7001(e)). \n\nWhile **\u00a7 7222(b)** mandates that a business provide specific, plain-language explanations regarding the purpose, logic, and outcome of the decisionmaking process, **\u00a7 7222(l)** serves as an enabling provision that allows businesses to go beyond those core requirements to offer context, such as comparative statistics, provided they do not violate other privacy protections.\n\nAdditionally, if a business has used ADMT with respect to a consumer more than four times in a 12-month period, it may rely on **\u00a7 7222(j)** to provide an aggregate-level response regarding the logic and parameters of the ADMT, which aligns with the regulatory intent of providing transparency through summarized or statistical data.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8111,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 33.683,
