    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7001(fff), 'train' means the process through which a technology discovers underlying patterns, learns a series of actions, or is taught to generate a desired output. This includes adjusting algorithmic parameters for ADMT, improving how a machine-learning model learns, and iterating datasets fed into ADMT.",
    "generated_answer": "Under California privacy law, the term \"train\" is defined in **\u00a7 7001(fff)** as the process through which a technology discovers underlying patterns, learns a series of actions, or is taught to generate a desired output.\n\nThis definition applies specifically to the requirements set forth in **\u00a7 7150(b)(6)** and **\u00a7 7153**. According to **\u00a7 7001(fff)**, examples of training include:\n\n*   Adjusting the parameters of an algorithm used for Automated Decisionmaking Technology (ADMT);\n*   Improving the algorithm that determines how a machine-learning model learns; and\n*   Iterating the datasets fed into ADMT.\n\nThe requirements concerning the training of ADMT apply only when the technology is trained using personal information (**\u00a7 7153(b)**).",
