  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7120_002",
    "query": "Does a company processing sensitive personal information of 60,000 consumers in a calendar year trigger the CCPA cybersecurity audit mandate if it also meets the standard CCPA gross revenue threshold?",
    "target_section": "7120",
    "expected_route": "HYBRID_BOTH",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": false,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.75,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Yes. Under \u00a7 7120(b)(2)(B), a business that meets the CCPA gross revenue threshold (\u00a7 1798.140(d)(1)(A)) and processed the sensitive personal information of 50,000 or more consumers in the preceding calendar year meets the definition of presenting a 'significant risk to consumers' security' and must complete a cybersecurity audit.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, yes, a company that meets the standard gross revenue threshold and processes the sensitive personal information of 60,000 consumers in a calendar year is required to complete a cybersecurity audit.\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7120(b)**, a business\u2019s processing of personal information presents a \"significant risk\" to consumer security\u2014thereby triggering the mandate to complete a cybersecurity audit\u2014if it meets the following criteria:\n\n*   **Revenue/Status Threshold**: The business meets the threshold set forth in Civil Code section 1798.140, subdivision (d)(1)(A) (the standard revenue/business threshold referenced in **\u00a7 7120(b)(2)**); **AND**\n*   **Sensitive Personal Information Volume**: The business processed the sensitive personal information of 50,000 or more consumers in the preceding calendar year (**\u00a7 7120(b)(2)(B)**).\n\nBecause 60,000 consumers exceeds the 50,000-consumer threshold for sensitive personal information, the business is required to perform the annual cybersecurity audit defined in **\u00a7 7001(j)**. \n\n***\n\n*Note: The provided text identifies requirements for both \"Cybersecurity Audits\" (\u00a7 7120) and \"Risk Assessments\" (\u00a7 7150). While this response addresses the cybersecurity audit mandate as requested, please be aware that the processing of sensitive personal information may also trigger separate \"Risk Assessment\" requirements under \u00a7 7150(b)(2).*",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9345,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
