  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7001_012",
    "query": "Does personal information of a 15-year-old consumer automatically qualify as 'sensitive personal information', and what legal standard applies if a business claims it did not know their age?",
    "target_section": "7001",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.1667,
    "key_term_recall": 0.6,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Yes. Under \u00a7 7001(bbb)(4), personal information of consumers that the business has actual knowledge are less than 16 years of age is classified as sensitive personal information. Furthermore, a business that willfully disregards the consumer's age is legally deemed to have had actual knowledge of their age.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, here is the answer to your query:\n\n### **Does a 15-year-old\u2019s personal information qualify as sensitive personal information?**\nYes. Under **\u00a7 7001(bbb)(4)**, \"sensitive personal information\" includes personal information of consumers that the business has actual knowledge are less than 16 years of age. Since a 15-year-old is under the age of 16, their personal information meets this definition, provided the business has the requisite knowledge.\n\n### **What legal standard applies if a business claims it did not know the consumer\u2019s age?**\nIf a business claims it was unaware of the consumer's age, the following legal standard applies:\n\n*   **Willful Disregard**: A business that \"willfully disregards the consumer\u2019s age shall be deemed to have had actual knowledge of the consumer\u2019s age\" (**\u00a7 7001(bbb)(4)**). \n*   **Actual Knowledge**: The regulation specifies that sensitive personal information includes information of consumers that the business has \"actual knowledge\" are less than 16 years of age (**\u00a7 7001(bbb)(4)**). \n\nThe provided text does not define specific protocols for how a business must verify age, but it establishes that the business is held accountable if it possesses actual knowledge or if it willfully disregards the consumer's age.",
