    "key_term_recall": 1.0,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "A request to know includes any or all of the following: (1) Specific pieces of personal information collected; (2) Categories of personal information collected; (3) Categories of sources from which data is collected; (4) Categories of personal information sold, shared, or disclosed for a business purpose; (5) Categories of third parties to whom data was sold, shared, or disclosed; and (6) The business or commercial purpose for collecting, selling, or sharing data.",
    "generated_answer": "Under section \u00a7 7001(nn) of the CCPA regulations, a \"request to know\" allows a consumer to request any or all of the following six categories of information from a business:\n\n1.  **Specific pieces of personal information** that the business has collected about the consumer (\u00a7 7001(nn)(1)).\n2.  **Categories of personal information** that the business has collected about the consumer (\u00a7 7001(nn)(2)).\n3.  **Categories of sources** from which the personal information is collected (\u00a7 7001(nn)(3)).\n4.  **Categories of personal information** that the business sold, shared, or disclosed for a business purpose about the consumer (\u00a7 7001(nn)(4)).\n5.  **Categories of third parties** to whom the personal information was sold, shared, or disclosed (\u00a7 7001(nn)(5)).\n6.  **The business or commercial purpose** for collecting, selling, or sharing personal information (\u00a7 7001(nn)(6)).",
