    "eval_id": "eval_7157_003",
    "query": "Are full CCPA risk assessment reports submitted annually to the CPPA by default, and how quickly must a business produce them if demanded by regulators?",
    "target_section": "7157",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.5,
    "key_term_recall": 0.5,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7157(e), businesses submit only summary information and attestations annually. Full risk assessment reports are not submitted routinely, but the CPPA or the California Attorney General may require a business to submit its full risk assessment reports at any time. Upon receiving such a request, the business MUST submit its full risk assessment reports within 30 calendar days.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, here are the answers to your questions regarding the submission of risk assessments to the California Privacy Protection Agency (the \"Agency\"):\n\n### Are full risk assessment reports submitted annually by default?\n**No.** Businesses are not required to submit the full risk assessment report to the Agency on an annual basis by default. Instead, businesses must submit specific **risk assessment information**\u2014a summary of the activity\u2014as defined in **\u00a7 7157(b)**.\n\nThis required information includes:\n*   Business name and contact information (**\u00a7 7157(b)(1)**).\n*   The time period covered by the submission (**\u00a7 7157(b)(2)**).\n*   The number of risk assessments conducted or updated during that period, broken down by processing activity (**\u00a7 7157(b)(3)**).\n*   Confirmation of whether the processing involved specific categories of personal or sensitive personal information (**\u00a7 7157(b)(4)**).\n*   A formal attestation signed by a member of the executive management team (**\u00a7 7157(b)(5)** and **\u00a7 7157(c)**).\n\n### How quickly must a business produce them if demanded?\nWhile the annual submission focuses on the summarized information described above, the Agency or the Attorney General may request the **full risk assessment reports** at any time.\n\n*   **Submission Deadline:** If the Agency or Attorney General requests the reports, the business must submit them within **30 calendar days** of the request (**\u00a7 7157(e)**).\n\n***\n\n**Compliance Note:** The submission of the summarized information under **\u00a7 7157(b)** is subject to specific timelines. For assessments conducted in 2026 and 2027, the submission is due no later than April 1, 2028 (**\u00a7 7157(a)(1)**). For assessments conducted after 2027, the information must be submitted no later than April 1 following the year in which the assessments were conducted (**\u00a7 7157(a)(2)**). All submissions must be made via the Agency\u2019s website at https://cppa.ca.gov/ (**\u00a7 7157(d)**).",
