    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7300(b), the Enforcement Division must notify the complainant in writing of any action taken or planned regarding the complaint, along with reasons for action or nonaction. Duplicate complaints submitted by the same complainant may be rejected without notice.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context in \u00a7 7300, the Enforcement Division handles notifications and duplicate complaints as follows:\n\n*   **Notification of Action:** Under \u00a7 7300(b), the Enforcement Division is required to notify the complainant in writing regarding the action, if any, the Agency has taken or plans to take concerning the complaint. This notification must include the reasons for that action or nonaction.\n*   **Duplicate Complaints:** Under \u00a7 7300(b), if the same complainant submits duplicate complaints, the Enforcement Division may reject those duplicates without providing notice.",
