    "eval_id": "eval_7001_005",
    "query": "Can an employer monitor an employee's personal social media activity or off-duty location tracking and classify it as evaluating 'performance at work'?",
    "target_section": "7001",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.5,
    "key_term_recall": 0.6,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "No. Under \u00a7 7001(cc), 'performance at work' explicitly excludes a consumer's location when off-duty or on breaks, as well as their use of a personal account (e.g., email, text messages, or social media). Personal account monitoring is only permitted if conducted solely to prevent/limit account use on company systems or to prevent confidential information disclosures.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory text, an employer **cannot** classify a consumer\u2019s personal social media activity or off-duty location tracking as \"performance at work.\"\n\nUnder **\u00a7 7001(cc)**, the definition of \"performance at work\" is limited to the \"performance of job duties for which the consumer has been hired or has applied to be hired.\" The regulation explicitly states that the following activities are **not** \"performance at work\":\n\n*   **Off-duty location:** A consumer\u2019s location when off-duty or on breaks.\n*   **Personal accounts:** A consumer\u2019s use of a personal account (e.g., social media, email, or text messages).\n\n**Exceptions and Limitations:**\n*   **Personal Accounts:** An employer may only involve a consumer's use of a personal account in the context of \"performance at work\" if it is done \"solely to prevent or limit the use of these accounts on the business\u2019s information system or to prevent the disclosure of confidential information\" (**\u00a7 7001(cc)**).\n\nThe provided text does not contain provisions authorizing the classification of these specific activities as \"performance at work\" for evaluation purposes. Note that the scope of this response is limited to the provided definitions in **\u00a7 7001(cc)** and does not address other potential labor or employment laws outside of this CCPA/CPRA context.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9079,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 7.988,
