    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.1667,
    "key_term_recall": 0.5,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7002(f), a business shall not collect categories of personal information other than those disclosed in its Notice at Collection. If it intends to collect additional categories or use data for incompatible additional purposes, it must provide a new Notice at Collection before collecting the data, and comply with all necessity and proportionality rules in \u00a7 7002(a)\u2013(e).",
    "generated_answer": "If a business intends to collect additional categories of personal information that were not disclosed in its initial Notice at Collection, it must take the following step:\n\n*   **Provide a new Notice at Collection**: Per **\u00a7 7002(f)**, the business must provide a new Notice at Collection to the consumer. \n\nAdditionally, the business must ensure that:\n*   **Compliance with Restrictions**: Any new collection or processing of personal information must comply with the requirements set forth in **\u00a7 7002, subsections (a) through (e)**, including the requirement that the collection, use, retention, or sharing of the information be \"reasonably necessary and proportionate\" to achieve the purpose for which it is collected (**\u00a7 7002(d)**).\n*   **Incompatibility**: If the business intends to use the personal information for purposes that are \"incompatible with the disclosed purpose for which the personal information was collected,\" a new notice is required (**\u00a7 7002(f)**).\n\nPlease note that **\u00a7 7012(d)** explicitly states that if a business does not give the Notice at Collection to the consumer at or before the point of collection, the business shall not collect personal information from the consumer.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9089,
