    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, I cannot answer your question regarding the definition of an \"insurance company\" under section 7270.\n\nThe provided text includes **Section \u00a7 7271**, which covers the \"General Application of the CCPA to Insurance Companies,\" but it does not contain a Section 7270. Furthermore, the provided text does not define the term \"insurance company,\" nor does it list specific entities included within such a definition.\n\n**What the provided context does cover regarding insurance companies:**\n*   **Applicability (\u00a7 7271(a))**: Insurance companies that meet the definition of a \"business\" under the CCPA must comply with the CCPA for any personal information that is not subject to the Insurance Code and its regulations. \n*   **Exclusions (\u00a7 7271(a) and (b)(3))**: Personal information collected in connection with an \"insurance transaction\" (as defined in Insurance Code section 791.02) or used to service an insurance policy is subject to the Insurance Code and its regulations, and therefore not subject to the CCPA.\n*   **Inclusions (\u00a7 7271(b))**: Insurance companies must comply with the CCPA for:\n    *   Personal information collected from website visitors who have not applied for an insurance or financial product (e.g., for targeted advertising purposes) (\u00a7 7271(b)(1)).\n    *   Personal information collected from employees and job applicants for employment purposes, which includes providing a \"Notice at Collection\" (\u00a7 7271(b)(2)).",
