  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7025_010",
    "query": "What privacy policy disclosures are mandatory for a business claiming exemption from posting 'Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information' links under frictionless processing rules?",
    "target_section": "7025",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7025(g)(2)(A)\u2013(D), the business must include in its privacy policy: (1) A description of the right to opt-out of sale/sharing; (2) An explicit statement that it processes opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner; (3) Instructions on how consumers can implement opt-out preference signals for frictionless processing; and (4) Instructions for any other available opt-out methods.",
    "generated_answer": "To claim the exemption from posting the \u201cDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\u201d or the Alternative Opt-out Link by processing opt-out preference signals in a \"frictionless manner,\" a business must meet the requirements set forth in **\u00a7 7025, subsections (f) and (g)**.\n\nIf a business chooses to process opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner, it must include the following specific disclosures in its privacy policy as required by **\u00a7 7025(g)(2)** and **\u00a7 7011(a)(3)**:\n\n### Mandatory Privacy Policy Disclosures\n*   **Right to Opt-Out**: A description of the consumer\u2019s right to opt-out of the sale or sharing of their personal information (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(A)**).\n*   **Statement of Frictionless Processing**: A statement that the business processes opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(B)**).\n*   **Implementation Instructions**: Information on how consumers can implement opt-out preference signals for the business to process in a frictionless manner (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(C)**; **\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(G)**).\n*   **Alternative Methods**: Instructions for any other methods by which the consumer may submit a request to opt-out of sale/sharing (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(D)**).\n*   **Scope Explanation**: An explanation of how the opt-out preference signal will be processed, specifically detailing whether the signal applies to the device, browser, consumer account, and/or offline sales, and under what circumstances (**\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(F)**).\n\n### Additional Compliance Requirements\nTo qualify for this exemption, the business must also adhere to these constraints:\n*   **Full Effectuation**: The opt-out preference signal must fully effectuate the consumer\u2019s request to opt-out of sale/sharing. If a business conducts offline sales that cannot be covered by the signal alone (e.g., without the consumer logging into an account), the business does not qualify for the exemption (**\u00a7 7025(g)(3)**).\n*   **Frictionless Processing**: The business must not charge a fee, change the consumer's product experience, or display notifications, pop-ups, or other interstitial content in response to the signal (**\u00a7 7025(f)(1)\u2013(3)**).\n*   **Notice Requirement**: Even if the business is exempt from posting the specific opt-out link, it must still provide the \"Notice of Right to Opt-out of Sale/Sharing\" within its privacy policy (**\u00a7 7013(e)(1)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8909,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 9.224,
