    "eval_id": "eval_7222_006",
    "query": "What statutory obligation do service providers and contractors have when a business receives a verifiable ADMT access request?",
    "target_section": "7222",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7222(i), a service provider or contractor must assist the business in responding to a verifiable consumer request to access ADMT, either by providing the consumer's personal information in its possession collected under contract or by enabling the business to access that information directly.",
    "generated_answer": "Under the provided regulatory framework, service providers and contractors have the following obligations when a business receives a verifiable consumer request to access Automated Decision-Making Technology (ADMT):\n\n*   **Duty to Assist:** Service providers and contractors are required to provide assistance to the business in responding to the request (\u00a7 7222(i)).\n*   **Provision of Information:** This assistance must include either:\n    *   Providing the business with the consumer\u2019s personal information that the service provider or contractor has in its possession which was collected pursuant to their written contract with the business; or\n    *   Enabling the business to access that personal information directly (\u00a7 7222(i)).\n*   **Contractual Requirement:** Per \u00a7 7051(a)(5), businesses must include provisions in their contracts with service providers and contractors that explicitly require them to cooperate with the business in responding to and complying with consumer requests made pursuant to the CCPA, including ADMT requirements under Article 11. \n*   **Enabling Compliance:** Contracts must require the service provider or contractor to either enable the business to comply with consumer requests or require the business to inform the provider of requests they must comply with and provide them with the necessary information to fulfill those requests (\u00a7 7051(a)(9)).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8907,
