  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7024_005",
    "query": "Can a business respond to a consumer's request to know categories of personal information by referring them to its online privacy policy?",
    "target_section": "7024",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Generally no. Under \u00a7 7024(j), a business must provide an individualized response. It cannot simply refer the consumer to its general privacy policy UNLESS its response would be identical for all consumers AND the privacy policy explicitly discloses all information required in a formal categories response.",
    "generated_answer": "Under the CCPA/CPRA regulations, a business generally **may not** simply refer a consumer to its privacy policy in response to a verified request to know categories of personal information.\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7024(j)**, a business must provide an individualized response to the consumer. It is prohibited from referring the consumer to the information practices outlined in its privacy policy unless the following two conditions are met:\n\n*   The business's response would be identical for all consumers; **and**\n*   The privacy policy discloses all the information that is otherwise required to be included in a response to a request to know such categories (as specified in **\u00a7 7024(k)**).\n\n**Important context regarding verification:**\nIf a business is unable to verify the identity of the person making the request to know categories of personal information, it may deny the request. In the event of such a denial, the business **shall** then provide or direct the consumer to the information practices set forth in its privacy policy (**\u00a7 7024(b)**).",
