    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7024(c)(1)\u2013(4), a business is not required to search for personal information if ALL of the following are met: (1) Data is not maintained in a searchable or reasonably accessible format; (2) Data is maintained solely for legal/compliance purposes; (3) Data is not sold or used for any commercial purpose; and (4) The business describes the unsearched categories of records to the consumer.",
    "generated_answer": "Under \u00a7 7024(c), a business is not required to search for personal information in response to a request to know if **all** of the following four conditions are met:\n\n*   **Format**: The business does not maintain the personal information in a searchable or reasonably accessible format.\n*   **Purpose**: The business maintains the personal information solely for legal or compliance purposes.\n*   **Commercial Activity**: The business does not sell the personal information and does not use it for any commercial purpose.\n*   **Disclosure**: The business describes to the consumer the categories of records that may contain personal information that it did not search because it meets the conditions stated above.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9245,
