    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7152(a)(9), the risk assessment report must document the review/approval date and names/positions of approvers. Crucially, an individual who holds the authority to participate in deciding whether the business will initiate the processing MUST review and approve the assessment. Legal counsel providing legal advice is explicitly excepted from being listed.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, the requirements for the review and approval of a risk assessment report are as follows:\n\n*   **Required Reviewer:** An individual who has the authority to participate in deciding whether the business will initiate the processing that is the subject of the risk assessment must review and approve the assessment (\u00a7 7152(a)(9)).\n*   **Documentation Requirements:** The business must identify and document the date the assessment was reviewed and approved, as well as the names and positions of the individuals who performed the review and approval (\u00a7 7152(a)(9)).\n*   **Rule Regarding Legal Counsel:** When documenting the individuals who provided information for the risk assessment, or the names and positions of individuals who reviewed or approved the assessment, legal counsel who provided legal advice are excluded from these documentation requirements (\u00a7 7152(a)(8) and \u00a7 7152(a)(9)).",
