    "key_term_recall": 0.4,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7302(c)(2)\u2013(3), participation in informal probable cause proceedings is strictly restricted to the alleged violator(s), their legal counsel, and the Enforcement Division. If an alleged violator fails to appear, they waive all rights to further probable cause proceedings under Civil Code \u00a7 1798.199.50, and the Agency decides probable cause based solely on the Enforcement Division's notice and arguments.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, here are the requirements regarding participation and non-attendance in a probable cause proceeding:\n\n### Authorized Participants\nUnder **\u00a7 7302(c)(2)**, only the following parties have the right to participate in a probable cause proceeding:\n*   The alleged violator(s);\n*   The alleged violator's legal counsel; and\n*   The Enforcement Division.\n\n### Consequences of Non-Attendance\nIf the alleged violator(s) fails to attend the probable cause proceeding, the following consequences apply under **\u00a7 7302(c)(3)**:\n*   The alleged violator(s) waives the right to any further probable cause proceedings under Civil Code section 1798.199.50.\n*   The Agency will determine whether probable cause exists based solely on the probable cause notice and any information or arguments provided by the Enforcement Division.",
