  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7220_009",
    "query": "Does a business need to issue a new Pre-use Notice every single time it uses an ADMT to allocate work to the same employee on a daily basis?",
    "target_section": "7220",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.4,
    "key_term_recall": 0.5,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "No. Under \u00a7 7220(e)(4), a business making systematic, regular use of a single ADMT (such as methodical daily work allocation to employees) may provide a single consolidated Pre-use Notice rather than providing a new notice to the same employees each time the ADMT is used.",
    "generated_answer": "No, a business does not need to issue a new Pre-use Notice for every individual instance of such use.\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7220(e)(4)**, a business may provide a consolidated Pre-use Notice for the \"systematic use of a single ADMT.\" The regulation explicitly provides the following example:\n\n*   A business may provide a consolidated Pre-use Notice to an employee that addresses the business's \"methodical and regular use of ADMT to allocate work to its employees, rather than providing a Pre-use Notice to the same employees each time it proposes to use the same ADMT for the same purpose.\"\n\n**Compliance Requirements for the Notice:**\nTo utilize this consolidated approach, the business must ensure that the notice meets all requirements set forth in **\u00a7 7220**, including:\n*   **Content**: The notice must include a plain language explanation of the specific purpose for the use, descriptions of the consumer's right to opt-out and access the ADMT, a statement regarding non-retaliation, and additional details regarding how the ADMT works and its output, as outlined in **\u00a7 7220(c)**.\n*   **Presentation**: The notice must be presented prominently and conspicuously to the consumer at or before the point of collection or before the business processes the consumer\u2019s personal information using the ADMT, as required by **\u00a7 7220(b)(2)**. \n*   **Format**: The notice must be provided in the manner in which the business primarily interacts with the consumer (**\u00a7 7220(b)(3)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8908,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 7.373,
    "retrieved_sources": [
