  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7222_010",
    "query": "What submission channels and design standards must a business maintain for receiving consumer requests to access ADMT?",
    "target_section": "7222",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7222(d), submission methods for ADMT access requests must be easy to use and free of dark patterns. A business may utilize its existing intake methods for requests to know, delete, or correct established under section 7020.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, a business must adhere to the following requirements regarding the submission channels and design standards for **Requests to Access ADMT**:\n\n### Submission Methods and Design Standards\n*   **Ease of Use & Prohibition of Dark Patterns**: A business's methods for consumers to submit requests to access Automated Decisionmaking Technology (ADMT) must be easy to use and must not employ dark patterns (\u00a7 7222(d)).\n*   **Use of Existing Channels**: A business may utilize its existing methods for consumers to submit requests to know, delete, or correct, as set forth in section 7020, to accommodate requests to access ADMT (\u00a7 7222(d)).\n*   **Verification Requirements**: Businesses must comply with the verification requirements set forth in Article 5 for all requests to access ADMT (\u00a7 7222(e)). \n    *   If the business cannot verify the identity of the requestor, it must inform the requestor that it is unable to do so (\u00a7 7222(e)).\n*   **Secure Communication**: A business is required to use reasonable security measures when transmitting the requested information to the consumer (\u00a7 7222(g)).\n*   **Account-Based Self-Service**: If a business maintains a password-protected account for a consumer, it may satisfy the access request via a secure self-service portal, provided that the portal:\n    *   Fully discloses the information the consumer is entitled to under the CCPA and these regulations (\u00a7 7222(h)).\n    *   Uses reasonable data security controls (\u00a7 7222(h)).\n    *   Complies with Article 5 verification requirements (\u00a7 7222(h)).\n\n### Required Disclosures in Privacy Policy\nRegarding the process for these requests, a business must include the following in its privacy policy as per \u00a7 7011(a)(3):\n*   A general description of the process used to verify a request to access ADMT (\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(E)).\n*   Instructions for submitting a request, including links to an online request form or portal, if offered (\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(B)).\n*   An explanation of the methods by which a consumer can exercise their rights (\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(A)).\n*   A contact for questions or concerns about the business\u2019s information practices, using a method reflecting how the business primarily interacts with the consumer (\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(J)).\n\n### Additional Notes\n*   **Aggregate Responses**: If a business used ADMT with respect to a consumer more than four times within a 12-month period, it may provide an aggregate-level response to the request for access (\u00a7 7222(j)).\n*   **Service Provider Assistance**: Service providers and contractors are required to assist the business in responding to a verifiable request to access ADMT, either by providing the consumer's personal information to the business or enabling the business to access that information (\u00a7 7222(i)).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.84,
