  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7220_008",
    "query": "When is an educational institution permitted to consolidate Pre-use Notices for automated plagiarism detection and automated exam grading?",
    "target_section": "7220",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 1.0,
    "key_term_recall": 0.4,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7220(e)(3), an educational provider using multiple ADMTs for multiple purposes (e.g., plagiarism screening tools for suspension decisions AND automated exam assessment tools for granting diplomas) may issue a consolidated Pre-use Notice to new students addressing all proposed ADMT uses.",
    "generated_answer": "According to the provided regulatory context, an educational provider may consolidate a Pre-use Notice for multiple Automated Decision-Making Technology (ADMT) uses under the following conditions:\n\n*   **Consolidated Notice Requirements**: Pursuant to **\u00a7 7220(e)**, a business may provide a consolidated Pre-use Notice provided that the notice includes all information required by Article for each of the business\u2019s proposed uses of ADMT.\n*   **Multiple ADMTs for Multiple Purposes**: Specifically, **\u00a7 7220(e)(3)** allows an educational provider to issue a consolidated Pre-use Notice to a new student when it intends to use multiple ADMTs for multiple purposes, such as:\n    *   (A) Software that automatically screens students\u2019 work for plagiarism to determine whether they will be suspended; and \n    *   (B) Software that automatically assesses students\u2019 exams to determine whether to grant them a diploma or certificate.\n\n**Required Content for Consolidated Notices:**\nRegardless of consolidation, the notice must adhere to the requirements set forth in **\u00a7 7220(c)**, which includes:\n*   A plain language explanation of each specific purpose for using the ADMT (**\u00a7 7220(c)(1)**);\n*   A description of the consumer's right to opt-out of ADMT and how to submit a request (**\u00a7 7220(c)(2)**);\n*   A description of the consumer's right to access ADMT and how to submit a request (**\u00a7 7220(c)(3)**);\n*   A statement that the business is prohibited from retaliating against consumers for exercising their CCPA rights (**\u00a7 7220(c)(4)**); and\n*   Additional information regarding how the ADMT works, the categories of personal information used, the types of outputs generated, and the alternative process available if a consumer opts out (**\u00a7 7220(c)(5)**).\n\nThe provided text does not define specific timing requirements beyond stating the notice must be provided \"at or before the point when the business collects the consumer\u2019s personal information that the business plans to process using ADMT\" (**\u00a7 7220(b)(2)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9035,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 8.719,
    "retrieved_sources": [
