    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7155(a)(2), at least once every three years, a business must review and update as necessary its risk assessments to ensure that they remain accurate in accordance with Article 10 requirements.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the statutory comparative context provided, here is the analysis regarding the frequency of risk assessment updates:\n\n**Analysis of Statutory Evolution**\nThe provided text contains only the definition of \"CCPA\" (\u00a7 7001(g) in 2023; \u00a7 7001(h) in 2026). The wording of this definition remains **unchanged** between the 2023 and 2026 versions, with only the citation (section number) being relettered due to the addition of other definitions in the 2026 text.\n\n**Response to Your Query**\nThe provided statutory context **does not contain** the provisions governing the frequency of risk assessment updates (typically found in the sections regarding \"Risk Assessments\" or \"Cybersecurity Audits\"). \n\nBecause the provided text is limited strictly to the definition of \"CCPA,\" there is no information available in this specific comparative context to answer your question regarding the frequency of reviews or updates for risk assessments. You would need to consult the specific sections of the regulations governing \"Risk Assessments\" (e.g., \u00a7 7150 et seq.) to determine the requirements for periodic review in the absence of material changes.",
