    "key_term_recall": 0.8333,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7001(eee), 'systematic observation' means methodical and regular or continuous observation. Examples include Wi-Fi or Bluetooth tracking, radio frequency identification (RFID), drones, video or audio recording or live-streaming, physical or biological identification/profiling technologies, geofencing, location trackers, and license-plate recognition (LPR).",
    "generated_answer": "Under CCPA regulations, **\u201csystematic observation\u201d** is defined as methodical and regular or continuous observation (\u00a7 7001(eee)).\n\nThe following technologies and surveillance methods are classified under this definition:\n\n*   **Tracking technologies:** Wi-Fi or Bluetooth tracking, and location trackers (\u00a7 7001(eee)).\n*   **Identification and profiling:** Technologies that enable physical or biological identification or profiling (\u00a7 7001(eee)).\n*   **Surveillance hardware:** Drones, video or audio recording, and live-streaming (\u00a7 7001(eee)).\n*   **Digital and spatial monitoring:** Geofencing, radio frequency identification (RFID), and license-plate recognition (\u00a7 7001(eee)).\n\nThe provided regulatory context is limited to the definition of \"systematic observation\" found in \u00a7 7001(eee); it does not provide further application or legal obligations specific to the use of these technologies beyond this definition.",
