    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.4,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7025(f)(1)\u2013(3), processing an opt-out preference signal in a frictionless manner requires that the business shall NOT: (1) Charge a fee or require valuable consideration; (2) Change or degrade the consumer's experience or product functionality compared to non-signal users; and (3) Display any notification, pop-up, text, graphic, animation, sound, video, or interstitial content in response to the signal (other than displaying the signal status or a link to a privacy settings menu).",
    "generated_answer": "To process an opt-out preference signal in a \"frictionless manner\" under **\u00a7 7025(f)**, a business must satisfy the following three specific user interface and operational restrictions:\n\n*   **No Fees or Consideration**: The business shall not charge a fee or require any valuable consideration from the consumer for using an opt-out preference signal (**\u00a7 7025(f)(1)**).\n*   **Uniform User Experience**: The business shall not change the consumer\u2019s experience with the product or service. The consumer who uses an opt-out preference signal must have the same experience regarding how the product or service functions compared to a consumer who does not use such a signal (**\u00a7 7025(f)(2)**).\n*   **No Prohibited Interstitial Content**: The business shall not display any notification, pop-up, text, graphic, animation, sound, video, or any interstitial content in response to the opt-out preference signal (**\u00a7 7025(f)(3)**).\n\n**Note on Permitted Content**: While these restrictions are in place, **\u00a7 7025(f)(3)** clarifies that a business is permitted to:\n1.  Display whether the consumer visiting the website has opted out of the sale or sharing of their personal information.\n2.  Provide a link to a privacy settings page, menu, or similar interface that allows the consumer to consent to the business ignoring the opt-out preference signal, provided that this interface also complies with the three restrictions listed above.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9364,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 8.102,
