  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7051_003",
    "query": "How does a business's failure to conduct ongoing due diligence or enforce vendor contract terms affect its liability if the service provider misuses consumer data?",
    "target_section": "7051",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.5,
    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7051(c), whether a business conducts due diligence factors into whether it had reason to believe a vendor was violating the CCPA. A business that never enforces contract terms or exercises audit/testing rights might NOT be able to rely on the defense that it lacked reason to believe the vendor intended to violate the CCPA at the time of disclosure.",
    "generated_answer": "Under the provided regulatory context, a business\u2019s failure to conduct due diligence or enforce contract terms impacts its legal standing regarding its knowledge of, and liability for, a service provider's or third party's misuse of personal information.\n\nThe specific implications are as follows:\n\n*   **Impact on \"Reason to Believe\" Defense**: Whether a business conducts due diligence factors into whether it has \"reason to believe\" that a service provider, contractor, or third party is using personal information in violation of the CCPA and these regulations (\u00a7 7051(c), \u00a7 7053(b)).\n*   **Consequence of Non-Enforcement**: A business that never enforces the terms of its contracts, or fails to exercise its rights to audit or test systems, may be unable to rely on the defense that it did not have reason to believe that the vendor intended to use personal information in violation of the law at the time of disclosure (\u00a7 7051(c), \u00a7 7053(b)).\n*   **Right to Audit and Verify**: \n    *   **Service Providers/Contractors**: Businesses must include contract terms that grant them the right to take reasonable and appropriate steps to ensure the service provider is acting consistently with the business\u2019s CCPA obligations. This may include manual reviews, automated scans, and regular assessments, audits, or technical testing at least once every 12 months (\u00a7 7051(a)(6)).\n    *   **Third Parties**: Businesses must include contract terms that grant them the right to take reasonable and appropriate steps to ensure the third party uses personal information in a manner consistent with the business\u2019s CCPA obligations (\u00a7 7053(a)(4)).\n*   **Remediation Rights**: Contracts must grant the business the right, upon notice, to take reasonable and appropriate steps to stop and remediate unauthorized use of personal information (\u00a7 7051(a)(8), \u00a7 7053(a)(5)).\n\nIn summary, the regulations establish that active oversight and enforcement are necessary to maintain a defense that the business was unaware of a vendor's non-compliance. Failing to utilize the contractual rights to audit, test, or enforce terms undermines a business's ability to claim it was not complicit in or unaware of subsequent misuse of data.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9007,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 14.937,
    "retrieved_sources": [
      {
        "parent_id": "v2026_sec7051_p1",
        "section": "7051",
        "section_title": "Contract Requirements for Service Providers and Contractors.",
        "rerank_score": 0.495,
        "snippet": "\u00a7 7051. Contract Requirements for Service Providers and Contractors.\n\u00a7 7051. Contract Requirements for Service Providers and Contractors.\n\n(a) The contract required by the CCPA for..."
      },
      {
        "parent_id": "v2026_sec7053_p1",
        "section": "7053",
        "section_title": "Contract Requirements for Third Parties.",
        "rerank_score": 0.0959,
        "snippet": "\u00a7 7053. Contract Requirements for Third Parties.\n\u00a7 7053. Contract Requirements for Third Parties.\n\n(a)\nA business that sells or shares a consumer\u2019s personal information with a thir..."
      }
    ],
    "error": null
