  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7222_002",
    "query": "Is a business permitted to direct a consumer to the top of its general privacy policy when responding to an ADMT access request instruction requirement?",
    "target_section": "7222",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": false,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.0,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "No. Under \u00a7 7222(b)(4)(A), directing a consumer to the beginning of a general privacy policy so that they must scroll through other information does NOT satisfy the requirement. The business must provide a link that takes the consumer directly to the specific section of the privacy policy that contains instructions for exercising CCPA rights.",
    "generated_answer": "No, a business is **not permitted** to direct a consumer to the top of its general privacy policy to satisfy the instructions requirement for responding to a request to access Automated Decision-Making Technology (ADMT).\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7222(b)(4)(A)**, the following rules apply:\n\n*   **Requirement for Direct Navigation**: A business must provide instructions on how a consumer can exercise their other CCPA rights. To comply, the business may provide a link that takes the consumer **directly to the specific section** of the privacy policy that contains these instructions.\n*   **Prohibition against General Redirects**: Directing the consumer to the beginning of the privacy policy, or to a section that does not contain the required instructions, does not satisfy the requirement. \n*   **Avoiding Obstacles**: The regulation explicitly states that forcing the consumer to scroll through other information to find the instructions does not meet the compliance standard set forth in **\u00a7 7222(b)(4)(A)**.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8652,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 11.998,
    "retrieved_sources": [
