  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7011_003",
    "query": "What information regarding opt-out preference signals must be disclosed within a business's privacy policy?",
    "target_section": "7011",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": false,
    "precision_at_k": 0.1667,
    "key_term_recall": 0.4,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7011(e)(3)(F)\u2013(G), the privacy policy must explain how an opt-out preference signal will be processed (e.g., whether it applies to the device, browser, consumer account, and/or offline sales) and how the consumer can use it. If processed in a frictionless manner, the privacy policy must inform consumers on how to implement opt-out preference signals for frictionless processing.",
    "generated_answer": "To comply with CCPA/CPRA regulations, a business must include specific information regarding opt-out preference signals within its privacy policy. According to **\u00a7 7011(a)(3)**, a business\u2019s privacy policy must include the following regarding opt-out preference signals:\n\n*   **Processing Explanation**: A general explanation of how an opt-out preference signal will be processed for the consumer. This includes specifying whether the signal applies to the device, browser, consumer account, and/or offline sales, and under what circumstances (**\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(F)**).\n*   **Implementation Instructions**: Information on how a consumer can use an opt-out preference signal (**\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(F)**).\n*   **Frictionless Processing (If Applicable)**: If the business processes opt-out preference signals in a \"frictionless manner,\" the policy must include specific information on how consumers can implement those signals for the business to process them in that manner (**\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(G)**).\n\nAdditionally, if a business chooses to process opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner as defined in **\u00a7 7025(f)** to take advantage of the exemption from posting \"Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\" links, the privacy policy must also include:\n\n*   A description of the consumer\u2019s right to opt-out of the sale or sharing of their personal information (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(A)**).\n*   A statement confirming that the business processes opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(B)**).\n*   Instructions for any other method by which the consumer may submit a request to opt-out of sale/sharing (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(D)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9038,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 8.498,
    "retrieved_sources": [
