  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7027_004",
    "query": "What third-party notification obligations must a business execute within 15 business days of receiving a consumer's request to limit sensitive personal information?",
    "target_section": "7027",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.5,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7027(g)(1)\u2013(3), the business must within 15 business days: (1) Cease non-exempt SPI uses; (2) Instruct its service providers and contractors to limit SPI processing; and (3) Notify all third parties to whom SPI was disclosed before compliance to limit processing and direct those third parties to forward the instruction to downstream recipients.",
    "generated_answer": "Under California privacy regulations, when a business receives a valid request to limit the use and disclosure of sensitive personal information, it must comply by notifying specific third parties and service providers within 15 business days of receiving the request.\n\nThe notification obligations pursuant to **\u00a7 7027(g)** are as follows:\n\n*   **Service Providers and Contractors**: The business must notify all service providers or contractors that use or disclose the consumer\u2019s sensitive personal information for purposes other than those set forth in \u00a7 7027(m). The business must instruct these entities to comply with the consumer\u2019s request to limit within the same 15-business-day timeframe (**\u00a7 7027(g)(2)**).\n*   **Third Parties**: The business must notify all third parties to whom it has disclosed or made available the consumer\u2019s sensitive personal information for purposes other than those set forth in \u00a7 7027(m). This obligation applies to disclosures made after the consumer submitted their request but before the business has complied with it. These third parties must be directed to:\n    1.  Comply with the consumer\u2019s request to limit (**\u00a7 7027(g)(3)(1)**).\n    2.  Forward the request to any other person with whom the third party has disclosed or made available the sensitive personal information during that time period (**\u00a7 7027(g)(3)(2)**).\n\n**Summary of Timing:**\nThe business must cease the prohibited use and disclosure of the information and complete these notifications as soon as feasibly possible, but no later than 15 business days from the date the business receives the request (**\u00a7 7027(g)(1)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8446,
    "llm_judge_score": null,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": null,
    "execution_time_sec": 10.753,
