    "key_term_recall": 0.6,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7124(c), the written certification must be completed by a member of executive management who: (1) Is directly responsible for the business's cybersecurity-audit compliance; (2) Has sufficient knowledge of the cybersecurity audit to provide accurate information; and (3) Has the authority to submit the certification to the Agency.",
    "generated_answer": "To complete and submit the cybersecurity audit **Certification of Completion**, a member of the business\u2019s executive management team must meet the following criteria as specified in **\u00a7 7124(c)**:\n\n*   **Responsibility**: They must be directly responsible for the business\u2019s cybersecurity-audit compliance.\n*   **Knowledge**: They must possess sufficient knowledge of the business\u2019s cybersecurity audit to provide accurate information.\n*   **Authority**: They must have the formal authority to submit the business\u2019s certification to the Agency.\n\nAdditionally, when submitting the certification via the Agency\u2019s website, this individual is required to provide an electronically signed attestation under penalty of perjury, confirming they meet these requirements and declaring that the information provided is true and correct, and that the business did not attempt to influence the auditor\u2019s decisions or assessments (**\u00a7 7124(d)(4)**).",
