    "key_term_recall": 0.0,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7123(c)(4)(A)\u2013(C), the business must maintain personal information inventories (data maps, flows, tagging), hardware/software inventories, and enforce allowlisting (discrete lists of authorized hardware/software controlling what can connect and execute). It must also enforce hardware/software approval processes to prevent unauthorized devices from connecting.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, \u00a7 7123(c)(4) mandates the following controls regarding hardware and software inventories and unauthorized execution:\n\n*   **Inventory Management:** Businesses must maintain inventories of their hardware and software (\u00a7 7123(c)(4)(B)).\n*   **Allowlisting:** Businesses must utilize \"allowlisting,\" which consists of discrete lists of authorized hardware and software, specifically to control what is permitted to connect to and execute on the business\u2019s information system (\u00a7 7123(c)(4)(B)).\n*   **Approval Processes:** Businesses must implement hardware and software approval processes (\u00a7 7123(c)(4)(C)).\n*   **Preventing Unauthorized Connections:** Businesses must prevent the connection of unauthorized hardware and devices to the business\u2019s information system (\u00a7 7123(c)(4)(C)).\n\nPlease note that the provided text is labeled as \u00a7 7123(4) rather than \u00a7 7123(c)(4), but it represents the specific requirements for hardware/software inventory and execution controls requested.",
